    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The one acceptance test `AcceptanceTest` is the real test (the other two files are an abstract base and a helper), and it verifies the new soft-match behavior end-to-end.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the possible-duplicate (soft-match) rule on `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**The rule:** a new owner that isn't a hard duplicate (its identity key is unique, still enforced) but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` while having a *different* normalized telephone is still created, with `possibleDuplicate` = true and `possibleDuplicateOf` = the matching owner's id; otherwise `possibleDuplicate` = false.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added two read-only fields to the `Owner` schema: `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32), so they appear on `OwnerDto` and serialize on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added persisted `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` columns with getters/setters (MapStruct auto-maps them by name).\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 added a `flagPossibleDuplicate(owner)` call right after the hard-duplicate check, plus the helper. It compares last name case-insensitively (consistent with the existing `countNamesakes`), requires both postcodes present and equal, requires the normalized telephone to differ, and picks the lowest matching id when several match.\n- **Schema SQL** \u2014 added `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of` columns to all four dialects (hsqldb \u2014 used by tests, h2, mysql, postgres).\n\nSeed owners carry no postcode, so they can't produce false matches. The first owner in the test (unique last name/postcode) gets `false`; the second (same last name + postcode 2000, unique telephone) gets `true` with `possibleDuplicateOf` pointing at the first.",
